    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "Given the problem: $\\left\\lceil-\\sqrt{\\frac{49}{4}}\\right\\rceil$\n\n1. Simplify the expression inside the square root:\n\n   \\[\n   \\sqrt{\\frac{49}{4}} = \\frac{\\sqrt{49}}{\\sqrt{4}}\n   \\]\n   \n   Since $\\sqrt{49} = 7$ and $\\sqrt{4} = 2$, we have:\n\n   \\[\n   \\sqrt{\\frac{49}{4}} = \\frac{7}{2}\n   \\]\n\n2. Substitute the simplified result back into the original problem:\n\n   \\[\n   -\\sqrt{\\frac{49}{4}} = -\\frac{7}{2}\n   \\]\n\n3. Determine the ceiling value of $-\\frac{7}{2}$:\n\n   - $\\frac{7}{2}$ is a positive number greater than 3 but less than 4.\n\n   - The floor value of $\\frac{7}{2}$ is $\\left\\lfloor \\frac{7}{2} \\right\\rfloor = 3$.\n\n4. The ceiling of a negative number is simply the negative of its floor. Hence:\n\n   \\[\n   \\left\\lceil -\\frac{7}{2} \\right\\rceil = -\\left\\lfloor \\frac{7}{2} \\right\\rfloor\n   \\]\n\n5. Therefore:\n\n   \\[\n   \\left\\lceil -\\sqrt{\\frac{49}{4}} \\right\\rceil = -3\n   \\]\n\nConclusion:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{-3}\n\\]",
